      "proposed_content": "Finite-prime minimizers with line-supported zeros and eventual hyperbolicity at each fixed Jensen degree are strong finite-regime facts with different unresolved global passages. The first requires suitable holomorphic convergence before Hurwitz can transfer zero geometry; the second does not provide the simultaneous all-degree control required by the RH equivalence.",
